. Weight: 8.9% debt / 91.1% equity (at market).\n\u2022 WACC = 0.911 \u00d7 9.83% + 0.089 \u00d7 1.0% = 9.04% \u2192 rounded to 9.0%.\n\n3-C. DCF valuation (WACC 9.0%, terminal growth 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 \u2264 nominal GDP]):\n\u2022 PV(FY26 FCF $188M) = 188/1.09 = $172.5M\n\u2022 PV(FY27 $272M) = 272/1.09\u00b2 = $229.0M\n\u2022 PV(FY28 $346M) = 346/1.09\u00b3 = $267.2M\n\u2022 PV(FY29 $425M) = 425/1.09\u2074 = $301.1M\n\u2022 PV(FY30 $492M) = 492/1.09\u2075 = $319.7M\n\u2022 TV = 492\u00d71.03/(0.09-0.03) = $9,088M; PV = $5,906M\n\u2022 EV = $7,195M\n\u2022 Net cash: cash $202M (pack, FY25) + short-term investments (post-2019 not disclosed \u2192\n  conservative $0) - LT debt $3M + assumed $800M convert proceeds now closed (cash +\n  $800M, debt + $800M \u2192 net $0) \u2192 NET CASH \u2248 $200M [Assumption]\n\u2022 Equity value = $7,395M\n\u2022 Per ADS (36.7M diluted): $201.5\n\nAt WACC 8.5%, TG 3.5% (the generous end): IV = $225-230/ADS.\nAt WACC 9.5%, TG 2.5% (the strict end): IV = $175-180/ADS.\nBase IV point: $210-225; point estimate $215 [Estimate].\n\n3-D. Cross-check multiples (not valuation alone):\n\u2022 FY26E EPS $9.20 \u00d7 28x justified P/E (for +100% revenue growth, PEG = 0.28) = $257.6\n\u2022 FY26E EPS $9.20 \u00d7 24x (normalized-tech P/E) = $220.8\n\u2022 FY27E EPS $10.22 \u00d7 22x (mid-cycle quality) = $224.8\n\u2022 P/E on trailing GAAP (vendor): 31.45x \u2192 overvalued on trailing; fair on forward.\nCross-check median \u2248 $225 \u2192 consistent with DCF IV $215. The market is paying ~$258,\nroughly 15-20% above my fair-value median.\n\n3-E. Reverse DCF: To justify $258 (market cap $8.67B), with WACC 9% and TG 3%, the\nmarket implies steady-state FCF \u2248 $8.67B \u00d7 6% \u2248 $520M by FY28-29. My base case reaches\n$425M (FY29); my bull case reaches $600M+. Thus the market is pricing a ~70% probability\nof the bull trajectory \u2014 optimistic.\n\n3-X. Tornado (top-3 variables by \u00b11\u03c3 impact on IV):\n\u2022 WACC (8.5%